  "details": "As suggested in great detail there : https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/images-store-exifiptc-metadata-for-images-taken\n\nI emphasize on the great usefulness of storing the DateTime of when the photo was taken in the DateTimeOriginal field of the EXIF Metadata of the file.\n\n+ All photography software (editing, archiving) rely on this info to order pictures chronologically, otherwise they have to rely on file creation time (does not goes well with copies, tranfers..)\n\n+ Stays there when the file is renamed/copied/modified\n\n- \"Hidden\" metadata that sticks to the image, but so is Author and World\n\nThank you",
